{"records":[{"id":"rhsw3nbjhz","title":"Essential gene profiles for human pluripotent stem cells identify uncharacterized genes and substrate dependencies. Mair et al.","description":"Human pluripotent stem cells (hPSCs) provide an invaluable tool for modeling diseases and hold promise for regenerative medicine. For understanding pluripotency and lineage differentiation mechanisms, a critical first step involves systematically cataloging genes that are indispensable for hPSC maintenance and proliferation. To map genetic determinants of hPSC fitness, we performed genome-scale loss-of-function screens in an inducible Cas9 H1 hPSC line cultured on feeder cells and feeder-free to identify essential genes. Among these, we found FOXH1 and VENTX, genes that encode transcription factors previously implicated in stem cell biology, as well as an uncharacterized gene, C22orf43/DRICH1. hPSCs essential genes are substantially different from other cell lines, and gene essentiality in hPSCs is highly context-dependent with respect to different growth substrates. Our CRISPR screens establish parameters for genome-wide screens in hPSCs, which will facilitate the characterization of unappreciated regulators of hPSC biology to understand the genetic wiring of hPSC fitness and pluripotency.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-01-24T11:57:50.932Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/rhsw3nbjhz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/rhsw3nbjhz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Barbara","last_name":"Mair","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jelena","last_name":"Tomic","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sanna","last_name":"Masud","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jason","last_name":"Moffat","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Stem Cell","Functional Genomics","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4wh82mxxrh","title":"Corresponding data of Supplementary Data 2  in paper \"Identification and Functional Characterization of Two Novel Hyaluronate Lyases BxHly33 and BiHly33, from the Human Gut Microbiome\"","description":"This is the raw data of Corresponding genome and dbCAN2 annotation results of Supplementary Data 2 in paper \"Identification and Functional Characterization of Two Novel Hyaluronate Lyases BxHly33 and BiHly33, from the Human Gut Microbiome\". ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-05-07T15:13:21.051Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4wh82mxxrh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4wh82mxxrh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"chengying","last_name":"yin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hina","last_name":"Sadiq","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wen-hui","last_name":"Liao","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hai-nan","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zheng","last_name":"Fu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Feng","last_name":"Han","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wen-gong","last_name":"Yu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Supplementary Lighting"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"r5s89w8g7k","title":"Whole genome of Lactobacillus helveticus MDC 9602","description":"Data shared to Manuscript \"Armenian functional food “Narine”: Characterization of fermenting bacteria Lactobacillus helveticus full genome sequences and potential functional food marker genes\".\nThe aim of this study was to perform whole-genome sequencing of the famous \"Narine\" functional food starter culture, establish the precise classification of the strain, and utilize genomic and proteomic data to reveal the essential probiotic and prebiotic characteristics of the strain.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-29T16:44:43.469Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/r5s89w8g7k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/r5s89w8g7k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Artur","last_name":"Hambardzumyan","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":null,"name":"Committee of Higher Education and Science of the Republic of Armenia","grant_id":"project № 21AG-2I090."}],"categories":["Functional Food","Probiotic Bacteria"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"239z62xt5x","title":"Data for: Genome-wide identification and characterization of R2R3-MYB family in Hypericum perforatum under diverse abiotic stresses","description":"Genome-wide identification and characterization of R2R3-MYB family in Hypericum perforatum","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-01-06T05:56:15.329Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/239z62xt5x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/239z62xt5x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhezhi","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lei","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yan","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wen","last_name":"Zhou","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Qian","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Evolutionary Biology","Transcription Factor"],"journal_issn":["01418130"]},{"id":"bpcpfns6vb","title":"Global genetic interaction network of a human cell maps conserved principles and informs functional interpretation of gene co-essentiality profiles. Billmann et al.","description":"Deciphering how genes interact within human cells is essential for understanding their functional wiring and the development of targeted therapeutic strategies. In this study, we present a genome-scale map of genetic interactions in the human haploid cell line HAP1, based on CRISPR-based perturbation of ~ 4 million gene pairs. The resulting network comprises ~89,000 high-confidence gene-gene interactions, organizing genes into hierarchical modules corresponding to protein complexes and pathways, biological processes, and cellular compartments, mirroring principles observed in yeast and highlighting the functional architecture of a human cell. This large-scale genetic network complements the DepMap gene co-essentiality network by capturing unique functional information, uncovering roles of previously uncharacterized genes, and identifying molecular determinants of cancer cell line-specific genetic dependencies. This study presents a general data-driven strategy analysis for systematically exploring the roles of genes and their functional connections in human cell lines.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-18T10:15:12.084Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bpcpfns6vb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bpcpfns6vb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Maximilian","last_name":"Billmann","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michael","last_name":"Costanzo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiang","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Arshia Z.","last_name":"Hassan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mahfuzur","last_name":"Rahman","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kevin R.","last_name":"Brown","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Katherine S.","last_name":"Chan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Amy Hin Yan","last_name":"Tong","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Carles","last_name":"Pons","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Henry N.","last_name":"Ward","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Catherine","last_name":"Ross","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jolanda","last_name":"van Leeuwen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michael","last_name":"Aregger","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Keith A.","last_name":"Lawson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Barbara","last_name":"Mair","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Amy F.","last_name":"Roth","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nesli E.","last_name":"Sen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Duncan T.","last_name":"Forster","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Guihong","last_name":"Tan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Patricia","last_name":"Mero","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sanna N.","last_name":"Masud","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yo